# Docker build context for research/model_arena_20260903/runtimes/<model_key>/Dockerfile.
# The context root is this namespace (research/model_arena_20260903/), so every
# Dockerfile's COPY sees exactly what survives this file.
#
# The one rule that matters more than any single line below: the build context
# must never contain benchmark data. No staged page renders, no ground truth,
# no evaluator output, no campaign receipt ever gets baked into an image layer
# -- an image is immutable and public-registry-hosted; anything baked into it
# is effectively published forever, unlike a gitignored local file.
#
# Verified against build/ignore_matcher.py's fnmatch-based simulation in
# tests/build/test_dockerignore.py (no new dependency; docker's own matcher is
# not available on this Docker-less host, so this file's *rules* are tested,
# not a real `docker build --dry-run`).

# Test code and fixtures -- never needed at runtime, and the arena repo's own
# tests import heavy fixtures no worker image needs.
tests/
**/tests/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# Generated campaign data (ARENA_CONTRACT.md section 1 layout). All of this is
# per-campaign-run state; baking any of it into an image would freeze one
# run's data into every future container built from that layer.
runs/
frozen_outputs/
queue/
scores/
receipts/
cost/
reports/
evidence/
failures/
tavonel/
.private/

# Every generated append-only or queue-state file, campaign-wide, regardless
# of which directory it lands in.
*.jsonl
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.tmp

# Local caches and VCS/editor metadata -- never part of a build, and some
# (.mypy_cache, .ruff_cache) can be large enough to blow the "context must
# never contain benchmark data" budget on disk alone.
.git/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/

# Top-level generated manifests/registries (ARENA_CONTRACT.md section 1): a
# worker adapter never reads these at runtime (its config comes from
# runtime.json baked at build time and the RunRequest at inference time), so
# they have no reason to enter any image.
/campaign_manifest.json
/canary_selection.json
/model_registry.json
/evaluator_registry.json
